  "_rules": [
    "The parser only has to return what Codka speaks: provider, currency, the amount and the sender's name.",
    "amount is exactly what the SMS says, never rounded: only thousands commas are removed ($12.5 -> \"12.5\", $45.25 -> \"45.25\", SLSH2,000 -> \"2000\"). It is a string so no decimal is lost, and Codka speaks it exactly like that.",
    "source 'real' = a real SMS with fake names and numbers swapped in. 'generated' = made from the same real format with other values; replace these with real samples from the market when you have them."
